      "round_summary": "Fix two assertion errors identified in round 1. (1) `state_must_change_every_cycle`: root cause is first-cycle false failure when `stato` and `RegNext(stato)` both equal StateA=0. Added `notFirstCycle` RegInit(false.B) guard that skips assertion on cycle 0. Preserved original assertion label exactly. (2) `U_reg_should_assert_within_8_cycles_after_reset`: root cause is that `LINEA` can stay high forever, creating an infinite A→B→F→G→A loop that never reaches StateE. Added fairness `assume(lineaHighCycles < 6.U)` constraining LINEA to go low at least every 6 cycles, breaking the infinite loop and allowing the FSM to reach StateE within the 8-cycle bound. Preserved original assertion label and bound. No homologous assertions exist for either fix.",
